---
description: ASD-STE100 nomenclature for all identifiers
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md` for every name you add or change.

Use ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English for files, modules, types, functions, variables, constants, components, CLI verbs, MCP tools, tests, and comments:

- One word, one meaning, one part of speech. A noun stays a noun. A verb stays a verb.
- Short, common American English. Three words or fewer in a compound name.
- Do not use two names for the same thing. Prefer the approved glossary in `AGENTS.md` (`Harness`, `Run`, `Context`, `Assembler`, `start`, `pause`, `cancel`, `fork`, `merge`, `inject`).
- No slang, jargon, clever metaphors, or opaque abbreviations.
- After you select a name, use that same name in the file, the type, the tests, and the HTTP/MCP/CLI surface.

Do not rename existing public names unless a human asks.
